 "claim": "The touching rule at every distance. In every Fano tree (a space built from Fano atoms alone by the creation map's splices), for the creation map (knots of up to three points, the four census far sides), a line a creates at a line b of another atom exactly when b touches its atom's cut toward a's atom: its atom emits at that cut, or b passes through the point its atom lost there. With the block lemma, the creation relation of every Fano tree is fixed by its tree. Proved: by PENDANT-LINE C the relation is that of the chain of their atoms; by PENDANT-LINE A creation at b is decided by the near side's relations on b's points and up to two further points; along a chain these are carried by the prefix's profile at each cut (its relations on the cut's three ports and up to two further points), a function of the previous profile and the next splice; closing under every splice reaches exactly 47 profiles, none new after three atoms; and on each of them, for every last atom and line, the two-round rule creates exactly when the line touches the last cut (12,894 of 12,894). Every profile leaves the three ports free, and the last atom alone decides creation.",
